CAT = "s63Securities"; SEG = "SEC"
Q = [
("Under the Howey test, an investment contract exists when money is invested in a common enterprise with an expectation of:",
 "Profits from the efforts of others", ["A paper certificate of ownership", "Prior registration with the SEC", "A guaranteed minimum rate of return"],
 "SEC v. W.J. Howey (1946) defines an investment contract as an investment of money in a common enterprise with an expectation of profits from the efforts of others. No certificate, registration or guarantee is needed."),
("Under the Uniform Securities Act, which of these is NOT a security?",
 "A fixed annuity", ["An investment contract", "A variable annuity", "A fractional interest in oil rights"],
 "The USA excludes insurance policies and annuity contracts under which an insurer promises to pay a fixed sum. Variable annuities are securities, as are investment contracts and interests in oil, gas or mineral rights."),
("A customer buys a gold futures contract on a commodities exchange. Under the USA it is:",
 "Not a security", ["A security", "An exempt security", "A federal covered security"],
 "Commodity futures contracts are regulated by the CFTC and are not securities under the USA. Options on securities, by contrast, are securities."),
("An unlisted company registering its IPO with the SEC usually registers it in a state by:",
 "Coordination", ["Notification", "Qualification", "Notice filing only"],
 "Coordination is the method for an offering being registered under the Securities Act of 1933 at the same time. Notification is for seasoned issuers, and notice filing applies to federal covered securities such as listed stock."),
("Registration by coordination generally becomes effective in the state:",
 "When the SEC registration does", ["Thirty days after filing", "When the Administrator signs an order", "At noon on the next business day"],
 "A coordination filing becomes effective at the same moment as the federal registration, provided no stop order is in effect, it has been on file for the required period and the final price amendment has been filed."),
("Registration by qualification becomes effective:",
 "When the Administrator orders it", ["When the SEC declares it effective", "On the second business day", "Thirty days after the offering"],
 "Qualification is the full state registration used when neither coordination nor notification is available. It takes effect only when the Administrator so orders."),
("Under the 1956 Uniform Securities Act, registration by notification becomes effective, if no stop order intervenes:",
 "3 p.m. on the second business day", ["Noon of the thirtieth day after filing", "When the SEC acts", "Only by Administrator order"],
 "A notification filing becomes effective automatically at 3 p.m. Eastern time on the second full business day after filing, or earlier if the Administrator allows. Noon of the 30th day is the rule for broker-dealer and agent registration."),
("Shares listed on the New York Stock Exchange are, under NSMIA:",
 "Federal covered securities", ["Registered by qualification", "Exempt only if sold unsolicited", "Subject to state merit review"],
 "NSMIA made securities listed on major national exchanges federal covered securities. States may not require them to be registered or reviewed on the merits, though antifraud authority remains."),
("A registered open-end mutual fund sells shares in the state. The state may require:",
 "A notice filing and a fee", ["Registration by qualification", "Merit review of the fund", "A stop order before sale"],
 "Shares of registered investment companies are federal covered securities. A state may require a notice filing, a fee and consent to service of process, but not registration."),
("Which is an exempt security under the USA?",
 "A bond issued by a city", ["Shares of a startup", "An unlisted REIT", "A limited partnership unit"],
 "Securities issued by the United States, states and their political subdivisions, such as a city, are exempt from registration. Startup shares, unlisted REITs and partnership units generally must be registered or qualify for a transaction exemption."),
("An individual sells shares of a private company to a neighbor, a one-time sale with no broker involved. This is:",
 "An isolated non-issuer transaction", ["A public offering", "A coordination filing with the state", "A primary distribution"],
 "An isolated transaction by someone other than the issuer is an exempt transaction under the USA. The shares need not be registered for that sale."),
("A customer calls an agent and asks to buy an unregistered, non-exempt stock that the agent never recommended. The trade is:",
 "An exempt transaction", ["Prohibited outright", "Allowed only after registration", "Exempt only for accredited buyers"],
 "An unsolicited non-issuer transaction through a broker-dealer is exempt from securities registration. The Administrator may require a written acknowledgment that the order was unsolicited, and the agent must still be registered."),
("Under the USA's private placement exemption, offers in the state during any 12 months may go to no more than:",
 "10 people, besides institutions", ["25 people, besides institutions", "35 people, besides institutions", "100 people, besides institutions"],
 "The limited offering exemption covers offers to no more than 10 persons in the state (other than institutional buyers) in 12 months, if the seller reasonably believes they buy for investment and no commission is paid for soliciting non-institutional buyers."),
("An offer of unregistered, non-exempt bonds made only to insurance companies in the state is:",
 "Exempt from state registration", ["Subject to qualification", "Barred by the antifraud rules", "Allowed only with an SEC filing"],
 "Transactions with banks, insurance companies, investment companies and other institutional buyers are exempt transactions, so the bonds need not be registered in the state for those sales."),
("A security is exempt from state registration. The USA's antifraud provisions:",
 "Still apply to it", ["Do not apply to it", "Apply only to listed stock", "Apply only if a broker sells it"],
 "Exemption removes only the registration requirement. Section 101's antifraud provisions apply to every offer, sale or purchase of a security, exempt or not."),
("An agent in State A emails an offer to a prospect in State B, who reads it there. The offer is made in:",
 "Both State A and State B", ["State A, where it was sent", "State B only", "Neither state"],
 "Under the USA an offer is made in a state when it originates there or is directed to and received there. This one originates in A and is received in B, so both states have jurisdiction."),
("A tombstone advertisement for a registered offering:",
 "A short notice of basic facts", ["Replaces the final prospectus", "May promise a set return", "Is a binding offer to sell"],
 "A tombstone is a limited notice giving the issuer, security, price and underwriters and where to get a prospectus. It is not a prospectus, makes no recommendation and is not an offer to sell."),
("Under FINRA Regulatory Notice 10-22, a broker-dealer recommending a Regulation D private placement must:",
 "Investigate the issuer reasonably", ["Register the offering with FINRA", "Rely on the issuer's statements", "Guarantee the issuer's claims"],
 "Notice 10-22 reminds firms that a recommendation requires a reasonable investigation of the issuer and the offering, including following up on red flags. Relying solely on the issuer is not enough."),
]
